From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:40:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvme: retry the post-M4 ANS start from off, and hand a
 running one over

A J604 (T8132) Stage 2 that Stage 1 handed a powered-off ANS found the
controller fatal after a warm reboot, with its CPU stopped (entry RUN=0
BOOT_STATUS=0x0 CC=0x470000 CSTS=0x2). The warm start got no HELLO and
left ANS down, so the inline payload had no disk and the boot stopped in
the proxy until a power cycle. The same image had started ANS on the
boot before.

Retry the start from off. A failed try is undone completely (CPU
stopped, its mail dropped, ANS and its PCIe block powered off), then ANS
is started warm again with 3 s for HELLO and BOOT_STATUS. On the T8132
the last of three tries also resets ANS through PMGR and boots it cold,
as Linux's apple,t8132-nvme-ans2 entry (cold_reset) does with a stopped
ANS. The first try is the warm start good boots took, unchanged.

If an inline payload's session still cannot be set up while ANS runs
with its firmware up and no fatal status, disable the controller, the
one fence for this stage's queues, and hand the session over: the
payload's U-Boot adopts a running post-M4 ANS. Only otherwise does the
boot stop in the proxy.

Assisted-by: LLM
